{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1785994851646305001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"romp-swath-wince","assignee":"","attestations":{"plan-review":{"algorithm":"HMAC-SHA256","author":"Iso Tester","head_sha":"eef3854547cd305ad0620cbb10568eeff77aacb8","key_id":"412fa5372ad877e0","kind":"plan-review","manifest":["plan-review: PASS","ticket: ff7d-34e8-9346-49a3","material: c6878313edba3580","model: claude-opus-4-8","runner: pydantic_ai","blocking: 0","advisory: 6","regver: 0dbaa5513314ac56","verified-at-sha:eef3854547cd305ad0620cbb10568eeff77aacb8","dep 399346b3a9f9d7149a3a68e0916cd9af21e1fa8685918fe94345d90aa13860a4 src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_errors.py","dep bf30c8a1fde1f58a3d780d864bb85dcb878d87388950393a92b2cc9d6533f8c5 src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/acli.py","dep 2ac29515a51f4074df8f2c33e8f15f44c043fa0318038e6428152cabe253915a src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/acli_subprocess.py","dep 0c60819c8c86059dc61172f94cd788c09ee7e4cead2f6fd7f6373da6538ff749 src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","dep e18bd88586f6002dd0b915874acaa5647225cb89f4faa67eb48db71cc504cb7b src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/batch_dispatch.py"],"signature":"d2e8ba5115116d017aa9f40984d188c43269aca4d5af8ced4f9ffc422a48fdd8","signed_at":1782668968747168000}},"author":"Iso Tester","authorship":{"signed":0,"unsigned":6},"authorship_ledger":[],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1782605235944438001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"RISK 1 (cross-session duplication). Two independently-authored modules each define their OWN `RetryExhaustedError` with a DIFFERENT base class, each raised by a separate retry loop and re-exported from a different public surface. A caller writing `except RetryExhaustedError` against one import silently MISSES the one raised by the other path — exception identity drives control flow, so this is a latent reliability bug, not cosmetic.\n\n## Why\nVerified ground truth: `acli_subprocess.py:124` → `class RetryExhaustedError(RuntimeError)` (re-exported via `acli.py`); `batch_dispatch.py:39` → `class RetryExhaustedError(Exception)` (re-exported via `applier.py`). So `acli.RetryExhaustedError is not applier.RetryExhaustedError`. `JiraAPIError` has ONE body (`batch_dispatch.py:31`) re-exported through both surfaces — only the re-export, not the class, is duplicated. The `acli` raise site chains (`raise ... from last_error`); the `batch_dispatch` site does NOT (`raise RetryExhaustedError(str(last_exc))` — drops the cause).\n\n## What — OSS-informed design (requests/urllib3/httpx/tenacity + PEP 3134)\nConsensus: one package-level base in a dedicated errors module; subclass `Exception` (or the single most-derived stdlib type a caller already catches); carry the last failure; chain the cause. `_errors.py` already exists (`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_errors.py`, ~67 LOC) — ADD the unified types there:\n- `class ReconcilerError(Exception)` — the catch-all base seam (per requests `RequestException` / urllib3 `HTTPError`).\n- `class RetryExhaustedError(ReconcilerError, RuntimeError)` — MRO `RetryExhaustedError→ReconcilerError→RuntimeError→Exception` is consistent and is caught by BOTH existing `except RuntimeError` (acli path) AND `except Exception` (batch path) sites, so NO call-site breaks. `__init__(self, message=\"\", *, last_exception=None, attempts=None)` — message-first keeps both current `RetryExhaustedError(\"…\")` call sites working; the optional fields mirror tenacity `RetryError.last_attempt` / urllib3 `MaxRetryError.reason`. Do NOT list `(RuntimeError, Exception)` literally (redundant/duplicate base — pylint E0241).\n- `class JiraAPIError(ReconcilerError)` — move the single body from `batch_dispatch.py:31` here, keeping `__init__(self, message, status_code)` verbatim.\nThen delete both `RetryExhaustedError` bodies and `import` the canonical one (`from rebar_reconciler._errors import RetryExhaustedError`); leave the `acli.py`/`applier.py` `__all__` re-exports (they now re-export the SAME object). Fix the chaining gap at `batch_dispatch.py:137`: `raise RetryExhaustedError(\"…\", last_exception=last_exc, attempts=max_retries+1) from last_exc`.\n\n## Scope\nIn: unify the two exception types in `_errors.py`, repoint both modules, fix the missing `from` chain. FOLLOW-ON (separate, not this ticket): consolidate the 5 HTTP/subprocess retry LOOPS (push/batch_dispatch/acli_subprocess×2/acli_rest) onto one `retry(fn, *, attempts, backoff, retry_on)` helper — linked as discovered_from.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `from rebar._engine.rebar_reconciler.acli import RetryExhaustedError` and `from ...applier import RetryExhaustedError` resolve to the SAME object (`is` identity test).\n- [ ] A `RetryExhaustedError` raised by either retry loop is caught by `except RuntimeError`, `except Exception`, AND `except ReconcilerError`.\n- [ ] Both raise sites chain the cause (`__cause__` is the last underlying exception); `last_exception`/`attempts` populated.\n- [ ] `JiraAPIError` defined once in `_errors.py`, `__init__(message, status_code)` unchanged; both surfaces import it.\n- [ ] Tests cover the cross-path `except` identity + chaining; existing reconciler tests pass.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_errors.py","reason":"add unified ReconcilerError/RetryExhaustedError/JiraAPIError"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/acli_subprocess.py","reason":"remove dup RetryExhaustedError, import canonical"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/batch_dispatch.py","reason":"remove dup classes + fix raise-from chaining"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/acli.py","reason":"re-export canonical type"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/applier.py","reason":"re-export canonical type"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","5ca8-5993-ca83-40f1"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"5ca8-5993-ca83-40f1","parent_status_uuid":"e8fe5514-c0b5-4d71-984f-1f40d5b23b66","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["audit-2026-06-27","oss-remediation"],"ticket_id":"ff7d-34e8-9346-49a3","ticket_type":"story","title":"Risk 1: unify reconciler exception taxonomy + chaining (OSS-informed)","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5c4f5e57-ec62-43ad-8a46-dab79d26bb8e","dcfc3df5-4aea-44b9-b0e4-c8f092fe0718","9f731903-d90a-4c4d-a0ee-e6604f6343f7","32ee6727-a3f8-4141-8a4d-6309693fb83b","e8fe5514-c0b5-4d71-984f-1f40d5b23b66","0f9808d8-b459-423a-b269-814a3732f0ce","b5bce67b-30ad-4b35-9641-08e5c32adee0"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785994851646305001,"uuid":"e58f9e1f-66fd-47b4-bff2-21dbc8a647ac"}